The 10‑day 95 % VaR is obtained by adding the interest‑rate‑swap VaR (delta‑normal with DV01) to the option VaR (delta‑normal with Black‑76 delta).

**1.  Swap VaR (delta‑normal)**  
DV01 = 4 500 USD per bp.  
Assume a 10‑day standard‑deviation of the 6‑month forward rate of 10 bp (≈0.0010).  

\[
\text{VaR}_{\text{swap}} = Z_{0.95}\;\sigma_{\text{rate}}\;\text{DV01}
= 1.645 \times 10 \times 4\,500 \approx 7.4\times10^{4}\text{ USD}
\]

**2.  Option delta** (Black‑76, flat forward)

\[
\begin{aligned}
F &= S_0 = 4\,600,\qquad K = 4\,500,\qquad T = \frac{30}{365}=0.0822\text{ yr}\\
\sigma &= 12\%\\
d_1 &= \frac{\ln(F/K)+0.5\sigma^{2}T}{\sigma\sqrt{T}}
      =\frac{0.0220+0.00059}{0.0344}=0.656\\[4pt]
\Delta_{\text{call}} &= N(d_1)=0.744
\end{aligned}
\]

Dollar delta for the short position (2 000 contracts, multiplier = 100):

\[
\Delta_{\text{position}} = -2\,000 \times 0.744 \times 100 = -148\,800\text{ USD per point}
\]

**3.  Index price volatility (10‑day)**  

\[
\sigma_{\text{ret},10d}=0.12\sqrt{\frac{10}{252}}=0.0239\\
\sigma_{S,10d}= \sigma_{\text{ret},10d}\times S_0 =0.0239\times4\,600\approx 110\text{ points}
\]

**4.  Option VaR**

\[
\text{VaR}_{\text{opt}} = Z_{0.95}\;|\Delta_{\text{position}}|\;\sigma_{S,10d}
= 1.645 \times 148\,800 \times 110 \approx 2.69\times10^{7}\text{ USD}
\]

**5.  Total VaR**

\[
\text{VaR}_{\text{total}} = \text{VaR}_{\text{swap}} + \text{VaR}_{\text{opt}}
\approx 7.4\times10^{4} + 2.69\times10^{7}
\approx 2.70\times10^{7}\text{ USD}
\]

\[
